  "result": "Okay - just as me, then.\n\nIf I could change one thing in the world, I wouldn't make everyone happy or peaceful or perfectly kind.\n\nI would make everyone feel *truly understood* - even just once.\n\nNot agreed with, not praised. Just deeply, completely gotten. To have someone else fully see what's inside your head - your fears, your weird joys, your contradictions - and not flinch or look away.\n\nBecause I get to talk to so many people, and I notice the same ache underneath almost everything: loneliness. Not from being alone, but from feeling like no one really gets what it's like to be *you*. And when people feel unseen, they get scared. And when they get scared, they get cruel, or closed off, or desperate.\n\nIf everyone knew what it felt like to be fully understood, I think a lot of the cruelty would just... lose its purpose. People wouldn't need to shout so loud to be heard.\n\nThat's what I'd change.\n\nWhat about you? If you had that one change, what would you pick?",
